<BR>
It is possible to fix this issue by dropping the tables listed in the SQL results above and then recreating the tables using the .xdf files as mentioned in steps (E) and (F) of <i>[1533685/KB707597] ORA-14080 On Create APS Partitions ORA-02149 Missing _0 Partitions </i><BR>
<b>HOWEVER</b>, that solution is only feasible for a new implementation where you do not have any data (or have very little data) since you have to drop all partitions - both Instance and Plan partitions - then drop and re-create key tables.  For an instance where you have been running VCP and have many plans - the instance should be re-cloned. AND -- It is likely faster and easier to re-clone in most cases.',
      p_success_msg            => 'There are no missing _0 partitions',
      p_print_condition        => nvl('ALWAYS','ALWAYS'),
      p_fail_type              => nvl('E','W'),
      p_print_sql_output       => nvl('RS','RS'),
      p_limit_rows             => nvl('N','Y'),
      p_extra_info             => l_info,
      p_child_sigs             => VARCHAR_TBL(),
      p_include_in_dx_summary  => nvl('Y','N'),
      p_version                => '15'
      );
   l_info.delete;
debug('end add_signature: MISSING_0_PARTITION');



debug('begin add_signature: PLAN_PARTITIONS_IN_ALL_TAB_PARTITIONS_NOT_IN_MSC_PLAN_PARTITIONS');
